<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Lesser Poland</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Małopolska</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Lesser <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poland">Poland</a> is a historical region of south-eastern Poland centred on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/krakow">Kraków</a> and the upper <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vistula">Vistula</a>. Added to the Piast realm by the 990s, it became the political heart of the kingdom, with Kraków as the royal capital. During the period of fragmentation after 1138 it was divided among duchies such as Kraków and Sandomierz.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/lesser-poland.jpg" alt="Lesser Poland" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: XEvansGambitx · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Zamek_Kr%C3%B3lewski_na_Wawelu_(6).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
